# {{name}}

A juiz component written in Rust. It was made with `juiz pkg create --idl` of juiz {{juiz_version}},
from the process / container declarations of `{{idl_main}}`.

License: {{license}}

## What is inside

{{types_table}}

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `{{idl_main}}` | The types and the declarations (JIDL). `build.rs` generates the Rust types of it |
| `src/lib.rs` | The Component. Each `#[juiz_component_*]` function is a type, listed in `juiz_component_manifest!`. Write the bodies (`todo!()`) |
| `build.rs` | Generates the Rust types of the `.jidl` (`juiz_idl`) |
| `app/app.conf` | The configuration to start juiz with. It is also the entry of the `.juizapp` package |
| `app/juizapp.yaml` | The `.juizapp` manifest (name, version, required juiz version) |
| `scripts/dev.sh`, `scripts/dev.ps1` | Build the plugin and put it in `app/plugins/<target>/` |
| `scripts/pack.sh`, `scripts/pack.ps1` | Build in release mode and make `dist/{{name}}-<version>.juizapp` |

## Requirements

- juiz {{juiz_version}} (`juiz --version`). Install it with `cargo install juiz_app --version {{juiz_version}}` or `pip install juiz-cli=={{juiz_version}}`
- Rust (cargo)

`juiz_sdk` and `juiz_idl` in `Cargo.toml` are pinned to the same version as juiz (`={{juiz_version}}`).
When you update juiz, update them to the same version.

